      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Even though your heartburn medication has helped in the past, experiencing such strong symptoms again warrants a closer look. It's possible that what you're experiencing could be another form of acid reflux or something entirely different. Self-prescribing stronger medication without evaluating the root cause could lead to side effects and other health complications. It’s essential to discuss these symptoms thoroughly with your doctor, even if you're currently on medication for heartburn, to ensure that nothing else is overlooked and to get the most appropriate treatment. Your well-being and safety should always be the top priority.",
      "source": "target",
